<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:35:34Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-sports" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-8171?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Who is drug testing Russia's athletes, now that they have returned to international competition?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:919eae9649440771979717b4469ca28c76958582b4812310c7ab2b65c5b5f98b</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:35:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T14:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-is-drug-testing-russia-s-athletes-now-that-they-have-returned-to-international-competition/a-79862467--23bc7b6e6570.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-is-drug-testing-russia-s-athletes-now-that-they-have-returned-to-international-competition/a-79862467?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">DW has found that three-quarters of Russia's weightlifting team had no independent out-of-competition testing before this year's world championships, despite the country's doping history.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Leading ice hockey nations, sponsors oppose Russia's return</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1237a22e8b81991e3b4407416c4a01bf87911c2bfdca6aac23d15fcb186dcb9</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T13:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/leading-ice-hockey-nations-sponsors-oppose-russia-s-return/a-79853742--b5324aaa0f6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/leading-ice-hockey-nations-sponsors-oppose-russia-s-return/a-79853742?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey's governing body says the impact of a court decision forcing it to reinstate Russia presents "significant practical and sporting challenges." Several leading nations say they won't play against Russian teams.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Cristiano Ronaldo announces retirement from international football</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8142c7ceefb1536f5ccd70f893903a17944f64058d3c7c6d2d7efbe9b56667b9</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:35:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T11:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cristiano-ronaldo-announces-retirement-from-international-football/a-79864361--825ad0ac29c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cristiano-ronaldo-announces-retirement-from-international-football/a-79864361?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The announcement by the footballing legend comes just weeks after a public spat with Portugal coach Jorge Jesus over playing time.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Gold for the West Bank: Meet Palestinian karate champ Mariam Bsharat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e12041533f118678ca4d05050817fcf719e681990a0232ced084e5cc7c6a7199</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gold-for-the-west-bank-meet-palestinian-karate-champ-mariam-bsharat/a-79851806--7b674acad5ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gold-for-the-west-bank-meet-palestinian-karate-champ-mariam-bsharat/a-79851806?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The occupied West Bank is not an obvious breeding ground for sporting success. But Mariam Bsharat, 17, has beaten the odds to become a karate world champion and is making a new life in Germany.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ice hockey officials considering options after CAS order to reinstate Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44ce58a7c670bcfde3d82020773a67590426d0208cb422f6b5bc196c70bb63d8</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-officials-considering-options-after-cas-order-to-reinstate-russia/a-79831451--d3d6cb0a329c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-officials-considering-options-after-cas-order-to-reinstate-russia/a-79831451?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey's ruling body is deciding how to respond to a decision by the Court of Arbitration for Sport that allows Russia back into international competition. Germany hasn't ruled out pulling out as a tournament host.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Bayern Munich's Kenya friendly highlights Africa's growing pull for global sport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80230c39b40ff0e9dcf2d1b9beb992f27a5784c2028bf99dcd5b88e8a9befc67</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T13:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-kenya-friendly-highlights-africa-s-growing-pull-for-global-sport/a-79796753--c6f4b50cf1c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-kenya-friendly-highlights-africa-s-growing-pull-for-global-sport/a-79796753?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bayern Munich are to open Nairobi's new Raila Odinga International Stadium against Ajax as Kenya prepares for AFCON 2027. The match highlights Africa's growing sports ambitions — and questions over cost and legacy.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Bayern Munich head coach Vincent Kompany's health scare highlights the need for better support for elite coaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1707c345dab6b759eb06bdace4c8ffb0b4571b93b57dbf312c03b1d2f1d09408</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T07:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-head-coach-vincent-kompany-s-health-scare-highlights-the-need-for-better-support-for-e/a-79764661--fcbaed2aac2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-head-coach-vincent-kompany-s-health-scare-highlights-the-need-for-better-support-for-elite-coaches/a-79764661?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Vincent Kompany’s health concern is a reminder that elite football's pressures affect coaches too. Better support, clearer structures and mental health safeguards are increasingly vital.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's first Youth Olympics open in Senegal amid hope and scrutiny</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb7c63eb3de4a7091a82ee1f82d2f8728f978ed47f97dbbc59c0ac209c2bdf29</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T09:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-first-youth-olympics-open-in-senegal-amid-hope-and-scrutiny/a-79760478--c3155dbcff43.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-first-youth-olympics-open-in-senegal-amid-hope-and-scrutiny/a-79760478?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Senegal is hosting Africa's first Youth Olympics, with 2,700 young athletes competing in Dakar, Diamniadio and Saly. The Games bring pride and hope, but also questions over cost, rights and legacy.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Harry Kane: Ballon d’Or for Bayern Munich striker</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc41635e1a6e488a8b1e55a25711648da8e210a6987277d86fa6c1fcc34feb4b</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T14:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/harry-kane-ballon-d-or-for-bayern-munich-striker/a-79723299--2a5c9f9ed870.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/harry-kane-ballon-d-or-for-bayern-munich-striker/a-79723299?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bayern Munich striker Harry Kane has won football's most prestigious individual prize, beating Kylian Mbappe and Lamine Yamal. Kane has developed even more in the Bundesliga despite an uneven league.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Manchester City, the UAE and the UK's PM in a political tangle</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5dfad5e34ba41d6e991522a8797c994285a5b7ed905808f4e2437ca985b22256</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T08:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-the-uae-and-the-uk-s-pm-in-a-political-tangle/a-79664729--9d27bb4511dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-the-uae-and-the-uk-s-pm-in-a-political-tangle/a-79664729?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nearly 20 years after arriving in England, Manchester City's UAE owners could exit amid cheating charges. That would pose a challenge for a city — and prime minister — closely tied to Abu Dhabi.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>FIFPRO report highlights growing pains in women's football</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8002135decd4c7b4f8d25697f55d99b0031310967d83abd5050d2e411b6f21a5</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T08:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fifpro-report-highlights-growing-pains-in-women-s-football/a-79648013--365fa34aee7b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fifpro-report-highlights-growing-pains-in-women-s-football/a-79648013?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Expected global revenue of over $1 billion and new faces at the U17 World Cup show women's football is booming, but a recent report also highlights need for better structures globally.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>World Cup 2034: Does Saudi Arabia shelving Neom Stadium spell trouble?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9fb167618da8f90391088dfb2ee3fc5d1ced141b663db7dacf6f201d697a7aa3</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T11:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/world-cup-2034-does-saudi-arabia-shelving-neom-stadium-spell-trouble/a-79592948--b8b608a266b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/world-cup-2034-does-saudi-arabia-shelving-neom-stadium-spell-trouble/a-79592948?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since winning the right to hold the 2034 World Cup unopposed, Saudi Arabia has been pulling away from sport. With reports that its most ambitious stadium project will be abandoned, what does this mean for the World Cup?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
